summary:
  Under the Bitrate chip every pass of a search is shown under the last, each sorted on its own.

history:
  Seen on 2026-09-23 with "nova radio": the name answer came back 320, 192,
  ... 64 and the word pass followed it with 320, 256, 224, so a 320 from
  Croatia sat under a 64 from London. Every answer now sorts the whole list
  once its rows are in; this takes the sort away.

target:
  package/contents/ui/FullRepresentation.qml

find:
              if (SearchLogic.asksBitrate(fullRepresentation._webLastQs)) SearchLogic.rateSort(webResultsModel)

replace:
              if (false) SearchLogic.rateSort(webResultsModel)

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_every_pass_of_a_bitrate_search_lands_in_one_order.
  Line-neutral.
